WEBVTT

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.030
The Kouka School of Musical and
Theatrical Arts' Culture Festival

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.870
is less of a "festival" and
more of a graduation show.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.450
The second-years show off
everything they've learned

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.370
in their two years at Kouka.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.540
Or so I'm told.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.540
Second-Year Lockers

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.460
Did you hear?

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.670
Apparently, the first-years are going to
be given some more time during <i>our </i>show!

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.930
That's right. I hear they're
going to act out a scene.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.470
A scene?! Who'd you hear that from?!

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:39.270
You should tell the teachers
not to let a pointless little skit

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.810
<i>ruin </i>our graduation show.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.610
It's just a rumor at this point.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.320
Don't look at me like that.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.320
Open your books to page 58.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.240
Okay, fine.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.330
Yes, the rumors are true.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.660
On the first day of the festival,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.630
the first-year class will have
15 minutes of stage time:

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.880
a ten-minute scene and a
five-minute choral performance.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.670
As I'm sure you've all figured out,

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:14.260
ten minutes is not enough time for
everyone to get to participate.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.640
So we'll pick four students
out of the 40 of you.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:24.060
The scene will be from the same show we
studied over summer, Romeo and Juliet.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.570
Same roles: Romeo, Juliet,
Tybalt, and Juliet's Nurse.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:31.860
Will you be selecting
the performers, Andou-<i>sensei</i>?

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.820
There'll be auditions.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.750
You have one week to decide
who you want to audition for.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.580
Then, you'll prepare for
auditions on your own.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.590
Those'll be held in two weeks.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.500
The person who gets the most votes
from the class will get the role.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.050
No voting for yourself.
Vote for whoever you think is best.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.840
And there'll be no hard feelings since
you're all voting for each other!

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.510
That's that! Open your textbooks!

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.900
"Baths"

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.820
So, are you guys all gonna do
the same roles as before?

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.740
Nope! I'm gonna play Juliet this time!

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.860
I'm guessing you're going
to do Romeo, Sawa?

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.320
I did Romeo before,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.620
but Sei Satomi-<i>sama</i>'s
Tybalt was super good, too...

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.790
Wow, you're not sweating.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.710
I am, actually!

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:53.840
I'm going for Romeo again. This audition
could be my foot in the door.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.590
Your foot in the door?

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.010
Yeah.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:01.010
For every performance after this, the
higher-ups will decide what role we play.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:05.810
I want them and the audience
watching me to remember me.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:09.690
I'm aiming for the top, and the
quicker I can get there, the better.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:14.900
I don't want to be part of the ensemble!
I'm dead serious about making it!

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.940
I'm not good at much other than singing...

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.070
C'mon! Thoughts like that are exactly why
timid actresses don't succeed, Aya!

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.040
That was too harsh, Kaoru.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.330
Way too harsh!

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.910
And not <i>everyone </i>wants to aim for the top!

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.920
Not all of us are like you, Kaoru!

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.080
Wait, what?!

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.590
We <i>won't </i>be at the bottom, though!

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:37.880
I-I wanna aim for the top, too!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.090
You're getting out already, Sarasa?

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.090
Yep.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.850
My goal is to play Lady Oscar someday.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.390
I don't have time to be
lounging around in the bath.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.150
I made all that fuss back there...

00:04:54.150 --> 00:05:00.610
...but still I don't know which
I should pick. Romeo or Tybalt?

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:01.530
Huh?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.160
Everyone's gotta have negative
opinions about my Tybalt

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.160
after what Andou-<i>sensei </i>said about it.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:15.170
And Sei Satomi-<i>san</i>'s <i>yandere</i>
Tybalt is still stuck in my head.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:19.800
But I don't think I should pick a role
just on what I'm more likely to get...

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.800
You know who I thought you
should've played this summer?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.930
You should play Romeo, Sarasa.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.140
You really think so?

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.020
Romeo is bright and warm like the sun,

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:34.810
and everything he does
is out of love for Juliet.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.900
He's a really simple character.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.820
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:43.200
On the other hand, Tybalt is this complex,
somewhat twisted character

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.280
who keeps his feelings
for Juliet hidden away.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.750
Does that mean... you think I'm simple?

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.960
Forget about that for a sec.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.630
Kaoru was right, this could
be your foot in the door.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:58.840
That, and...

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.550
I want to see your Romeo again.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.890
Did I just creep her out?

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.600
You're gonna make me blush
with a compliment like that!

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:18.810
Japanese Room

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:20.610
So the rumor was true, then.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.950
I'm assuming you're going
for Juliet, Narata-<i>san</i>?

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:29.120
I have a hard time smiling, so I
was going to try out for her nurse--

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.000
What the hell? Are you stupid?

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.790
I mean, out of all the randos
in the hundredth Kouka class,

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:41.130
the only girl our audiences want to see is
the one and only Ai Narata from JPX.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:46.470
And you want to play the nurse? Are you
trying to give them a heart attack?

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:50.180
Absolutely not.
You're going to try out for Juliet.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.770
Sure, but I didn't do
anything to earn that.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:58.520
You can develop the
talent to "earn" that later.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:03.360
But you were born pretty,
and that gives you an advantage.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.070
Even if you don't have
the talent to deserve it,

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:10.910
you're still starting closer to
the finish line than anyone else.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:14.200
All you need to do is run as
fast as you can to finish first.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.960
You missed a spot here.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.960
My word!

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:26.050
Those first-years are more stressed
out than I've<i> ever </i>seen them!

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.590
Must be 'cause you're
making them audition, yeah?

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.590
Yup.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.470
Teamwork's good and all
for performing together,

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.680
but it's good to stoke those competitive
flames every once in a while.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.980
Keep an eye on those teens, though.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:40.110
They may get a bit too worked up,
or too ruthless with their competition.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:45.780
Or too caught up in their jealousy
and anger. Be careful, now.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:46.990
Right.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.660
Do you know what you're
going for yet, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:53.870
Not yet.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.670
What's up, Akiya-<i>kun</i>?

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:06.510
I saw your tweet. You sounded
pretty hung up on your audition.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:10.800
Yeah. I don't know if I
should pick Romeo or Tybalt.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.430
I think you should do whatever
won't leave you with regrets later.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.980
Then I guess I should do Romeo...

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:19.730
Wait, lemme say that a different way.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.480
You should play the role that
you <i>want </i>to play, Sarasa-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.990
Aww, c'mon! That's the whole
reason I'm struggling here!

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:31.490
So if someone said you should do
Romeo and you're still not sure,

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.830
doesn't that mean you actually
want to play the other role?

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.870
"Romeo: Kaoru"

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.500
"Juliet: Chika Sawada, Chiaki Sawada"

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:54.130
"Juliet: Ayako Yamada"

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:59.180
Even if you don't have
the talent to deserve it,

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:02.020
all you need to do is run as
fast as you can to finish first.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.600
"Juliet: Ai Narata"

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:07.280
When Hijiri-<i>senpai </i>told me to
"run fast and finish first,"

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:11.490
she meant, "if you want to be top star,
you need to work as hard as you can."

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.740
"Tybalt: Sawa Sugimoto"

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:26.920
Wow.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.000
"Sarasa Watanabe"

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.590
"Tybalt"

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.090
I'm giving him another go!

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.760
Let's both break a leg!

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.350
Sorry, no handshake.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.600
Huh?

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:46.980
One facet of the Kouka Acting Troupe's
beauty is each troupe's team spirit.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:52.610
As such, as our class representative,
I strive to remain calm and impartial.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:56.660
But these are auditions,
and you are my rival, Sarasa.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.370
So there will be no handshake.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.500
Sawa got serious!

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.250
Okay. Then I'm gonna come
atcha with everything I got!

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.750
What did I <i>just </i>say about handshakes?

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:12.470
That day, I started off by adding the
readings to all the words on the script.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:17.600
Romeo... Romeo...

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:17.600
What's with the intense eyes?

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.560
I thought it'd help me get
into character or something.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.560
Think you can do Tybalt justice?

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:32.820
I tried to come up with ideas for <i>my</i>
Tybalt. Could you tell me what you think?

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.780
Sure, lemme see.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:38.740
"I yet live, my end cannot be so nigh!"

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.950
"My life ends by the hand of Romeo."

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.620
That's Basic Tybalt.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.920
O-Okay.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:52.590
"In my palm, is this a rose? Nay, 'tis the
red of lifeblood from my chest! Blood!"

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:56.220
"A curse upon you, Montague!"

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.600
That's Egotistical Tybalt.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:10:59.930
Okay.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:05.140
"Oh, Juliet! The star shining
bright in my dark sky!"

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.190
"No matter how many
billions of light-years I fly,

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:09.980
I will never reach you!"

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.190
That's Smart Tybalt.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.740
I've also got--

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.280
I don't think you can change the lines.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:21.160
But if I want to make it more original, I
feel like I have to change the lines!

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:25.790
If you make it <i>too </i>original,
it'll be overkill.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:30.000
What's important is <i>how</i>
you lose yourself in the role.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.340
The uniqueness of the performance
comes from the actor themself.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:36.340
I got a golden nugget of wisdom!

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.680
Well, I got it from someone else.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:42.680
Ugh, what is <i>with </i>this actress?

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:43.390
Huh?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:48.060
She's all "look at me, look at me!"
She's <i>so </i>overdoing it.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.310
You have to understand
the role you're playing

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.860
and figure out how to
lose yourself in that role.

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:55.900
Really, Mommy?

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.610
Really, Ai.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.740
Actresses like this one
don't last long in show biz.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:01.950
Wow.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:08.250
So here's a question for you. How do
you think Tybalt starts his mornings?

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:12.380
If you can figure out what his
day is like from the script,

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.130
then you should get an idea of who he is.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:21.140
I feel like Andou-<i>sensei </i>mentioned
something like that in class once!

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.390
Here's another question.

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:23.310
Okay!

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:27.180
What does Tybalt think
about when he's dying?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.980
If you can express that
without changing his lines,

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:33.270
then your performance will show
your unique take on Tybalt.

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:37.320
Okay. Sounds like I really
gotta think this over.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:40.530
Thanks for the tips, Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:41.620
Mm-hmm.

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:47.830
Where'd you learn all this, by the way?
From someone in JPX?

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.040
No.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:52.670
From an actress.

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:56.670
Romeo and Juliet is a famous tragedy
written by William Shakespeare

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.880
four hundred years ago.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:05.760
The story takes place in
14th century Italy, in Verona.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.520
The Montague family's only son, Romeo,

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:12.400
falls in love with the Capulet
family's only daughter, Juliet.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:17.070
They secretly marry, and though they try
to evade the forces pulling them apart,

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:22.570
their tragic tale ends with them
bound together only in death.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:27.330
Tybalt harbors an unrequited
love for his cousin Juliet.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:31.330
When he kills Romeo's
friend Mercutio in anger,

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.540
Romeo duels and kills him.

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:37.750
Romeo, you foul knave!

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.840
Ow. It hurts.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.340
I'm, like, dying.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:46.850
Hey, are you okay?

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:50.310
Is your blood sugar low?
What hurts? Can you breathe?

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:54.730
The sky Tybalt saw in his
final moments was so beautiful.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.940
What sky?

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:58.610
In a world this beautiful,

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:03.030
why was Tybalt so obsessed
with his anger and hatred?

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.780
Stop messing around and finish cleaning!

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:06.030
Yes, ma'am!

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.620
Our auditions are tomorrow, yay!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.080
You guys could at <i>least </i>make small talk!

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:21.050
Maybe Ai was right.
I should've just taken Romeo.

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:23.800
Auditions are tomorrow,

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:28.140
and I still haven't gotten any closer to
knowing how Tybalt feels when he dies.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.180
Come to think of it,

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:34.480
I've never hated someone, or had
a grudge against anyone, either.

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:35.900
Really?

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:37.610
Great question.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:42.070
My mother opened the door
for me to enter the kabuki world.

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:43.700
Shirakawa-<i>san</i>...

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:46.030
I was just a kid, so there were plenty
of times I didn't want to be there,

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:48.740
but now it's my whole life.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.540
Oh, I've gotta go!

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.540
Kabuki lessons again?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.550
Yeah. See you later!

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:06.890
Grandpa Ken, Akiya-<i>kun </i>left.

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:08.510
Is that right?

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:11.890
I hope Akiya-<i>kun </i>falls and gets hurt.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.180
Hey! Sarasa!

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:16.230
I know you want to play with him,
but you do <i>not </i>say those things! Ever!

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:20.480
You say something mean like that
and it'll come right back at you!

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:24.440
I didn't mean it! I really didn't!

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:28.490
I was just kidding!

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:30.200
I remember now.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:36.120
I was so jealous of Akiya-<i>kun </i>because
he got to be what I couldn't.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:42.630
For a second, I hoped he'd get hurt
and never be able to do kabuki again.

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:45.670
Something I wanted so badly,
but could never have.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:49.470
But Romeo took it
without a second thought...

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:53.520
Good morning!
Thank you for having us today!

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:57.310
Good morning, first-years.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:02.860
Wait, other teachers are going
to be judging us, too?

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:05.440
It's so mean that he didn't tell us...

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:11.450
Come up when I call your name.
The four of you will put on the scene.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:14.410
After that, each of you will
sing a verse of the song.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:18.790
We each get a vote, too.
Can't wait to watch.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.380
Mmkay, let's get started.

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:26.510
First group. Romeo, Manami Ueda.

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:27.800
Y-Yes, sir!

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:29.800
Juliet, Ai Narata.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:30.930
Yes, sir.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:32.930
Ai-<i>chan</i>! You got this!

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:37.770
Of the beauty I've seen,
none caught my eye,

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:41.480
save for the glimmering jewel...

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:44.150
The glimmering jewel...

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:48.190
I'm sorry, can I try that one more time?

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:51.030
Go ahead. From the top, please.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.740
This hellish pressure is soul-crushing...

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:58.790
Doesn't seem to be affecting Naracchi,
though. Of course this is easy for her.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:02.080
It's not that this is easy.
I'm just used to it.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:06.170
When I was an idol, I got used to
ignoring being the center of attention.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:09.720
Despite that, when I was on bigger stages,

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:13.800
there were times when the nerves
and pressure really got to me.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.890
They're getting to me now, too...

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:21.770
...because I still have no idea
what "love" feels like.

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.940
You have to understand
the role you're playing

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:27.030
and lose yourself in that role.

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:29.530
I went and said that to
Sarasa with a straight face,

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:32.780
but now it's coming back
to bite me in the butt.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:35.410
I couldn't lose myself in my role at all.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.750
Of the beauty I've seen,
none caught my eye,

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:43.120
save for the glimmering
jewel that is hers!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.500
After Romeo's soliloquy is done,
it's Juliet's turn to speak.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.840
Now I am held, imprisoned in her shine,

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:49.630
and my eyes will be caught by no other.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.630
Love. What is love?

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:54.470
Ai-<i>chan</i>'s eyes are totally glazing over,
don't you think? She's not even blinking.

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:57.220
You think so? She looks
the same as ever to me.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.310
But she's not.

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:01.810
Ai-<i>chan </i>might be bad at expressing
her feelings on the outside,

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:05.770
but on the inside, they're always
running at a hundred miles an hour.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:10.610
One day, out of nowhere,
Juliet fell head over heels in love.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.280
It was love at first sight, right?

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:16.950
Does that mean his looks were important?
She fell for him because he was hot?

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.700
Can two people be soulmates after
falling for each other like that?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.830
It couldn't have just been his looks.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.250
There's gotta be a more convincing reason.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:27.880
Were they on the same wavelength?
Was it Romeo's aura or something?

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:31.130
If you love someone, can you
see their aura? Did she have ESP?

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.670
Is love something out of science fiction?!

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.840
I have no idea, and I have to think fast!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:39.310
At the very least,
I just need to say the lines.

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.850
No, I can't give up here!

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.940
If I stumble here, I won't be
able to climb up to the top.

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:52.320
With what words should I profess
my deepest love for you?

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.320
And Romeo's soliloquy is almost over!

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:53.950
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.320
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:02.160
Help! These guys won't leave us alone!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.000
But even if you can't forget
something that happened,

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:07.830
you can make new memories by having fun

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.840
and being passionate about
the things you love.

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:13.840
Just keep overwriting the bad
memories with lots of good ones,

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:17.590
and eventually, the bad
ones will fade away.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:22.100
Look! Upon the pitch-black
curtain of night...

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:24.730
...sparkle a thousand brilliant stars!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:34.150
I want to be friends with you,
Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.950
I'm so glad!

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:41.620
Ever since the first moment
I met you, Ai-<i>chan</i>,

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:44.330
I knew I wanted to be friends with you!

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:53.840
O Romeo! Wherefore art thou Romeo?

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:59.220
Deny thy father and refuse thy name;

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:03.350
Or, if thou wilt not, be but sworn my
love, and I'll no longer be a Capulet.

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:08.650
I still don't know what love is.
Maybe one day, I will.

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:11.980
I might lack confidence in myself now,

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:16.400
but the moment we met in the fluttering
petals beneath the cherry tree...

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:19.200
...is a moment I'll never forget.

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:23.370
That precious moment will guide me

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:27.330
to cross the silver bridge with Sarasa.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:33.090
And if I want to do that, I can't
give up, not now, not ever.

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:36.970
Amidst the sea-swells
of the thronging crowd,

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.880
Romeo,

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:43.890
t'was your face the light endow'd!

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:54.900
Thank you. Let's take a five-minute break
before we start with our next group.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:56.650
You were so good, Naracchi!

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:59.360
You totally gave me goosebumps!

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:05.040
That was incredible! You blew me away!

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:08.830
What did you do to shed
such beautiful tears?!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.040
Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:15.920
Welcome back!

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:19.220
I-I'm back.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:23.680
Oh, no... The first Juliet was so amazing.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:28.770
Maybe I'm really <i>not </i>cut out for
Juliet after all. What should I do?

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:32.690
You still haven't stopped doing that, Aya?

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:33.400
Huh?

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:36.780
You need to stop whining all the time.

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:39.610
Because this late in the game,

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:43.110
<i>everyone </i>is thinking that,
they just don't say it!

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:49.290
Okay, next group. Romeo, Hitomi Konno.

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:50.660
Yes, sir!

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:52.580
Juliet, Ayako Yamada.

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:54.080
Y-Yes, sir!

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.090
Tybalt, Sawa Sugimoto.

00:21:56.090 --> 00:21:57.590
Yes, sir!

00:21:57.590 --> 00:21:59.550
Juliet's Nurse, Keito Mochida.

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:00.720
Yes, sir!

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:09.390
Break a leg, Sugimoto-<i>san</i>, Aya-<i>chan</i>!

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:46.980
Act 12: 
